<section class="qualification" id="for-you" aria-labelledby="qualification-title">
	<div class="qualification__container">
		<header class="qualification__intro">
			<h2 class="qualification__title" id="qualification-title">Is this book for you?</h2>
			<p>
				It assumes you can already write HTML and CSS. It helps you decide when modern CSS can do the job
				before you reach for JavaScript.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="qualification__layout">
			<div class="qualification__fit">
				<h3 class="qualification__subtitle">You’ll get the most from it if</h3>
				<ul class="qualification__list qualification__list--fit">
					<li>You reach for JavaScript out of habit, not because the problem needs it.</li>
					<li>You know CSS well enough to know it moved on without you.</li>
					<li>You maintain components that feel heavier than what they do.</li>
					<li>You care about accessibility, performance, and resilient interfaces.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<aside class="qualification__skip">
				<h3 class="qualification__subtitle">Skip it if</h3>
				<ul class="qualification__list">
					<li>You have never written HTML or CSS before.</li>
					<li>You are looking for a React or framework tutorial.</li>
					<li>You want theory rather than practical, buildable patterns.</li>
				</ul>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
